WEBVTT

NOTE Source-grounded narration; diagrams are editorial, not source data.

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:07.550
On the proposal, the final structure was an imidazopyridine. The

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:14.550
scheme had a destination before we had made the molecule.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:24.050
Our team proposed two synthetic routes toward substituted imidazopyridines, with structural characterization

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:32.550
to come before biological evaluation. That was the plan in 2018.

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:43.050
By the final report, we could not claim the intended heterocycles. The proposed ring

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:52.550
closure had not delivered those compounds. Whatever we wrote next had to begin there.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:01:02.050
We did isolate and characterize three imines, also called Schiff bases. They had

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:10.550
entered the project as intermediates, not the endpoint we were originally pursuing.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:19.550
Instead of treating those compounds only as unfinished starting materials, we examined their

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:27.550
response to anions. Cyanide produced a particularly visible change in one sensor solution.

00:01:28.550 --> 00:01:37.050
Under the reported test conditions, a yellow solution turned orange after cyanide was added.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:45.550
A colour change was observable. Its meaning still had to be checked spectroscopically.

00:01:46.550 --> 00:01:55.050
The band near 380 nanometres declined as a new band near 450 grew. The report gave

00:01:55.050 --> 00:02:03.550
a detection limit of 1.42 times ten to the minus five molar for that sensor.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:14.050
Colleagues explored two compounds, CMP5 and CMPB, in triple-negative breast-cancer cell lines. Some proliferation

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:23.550
and migration readouts differed, but that was not evidence of a validated treatment.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:33.050
Some c-MYC measurements rose where we had expected the opposite, and some

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:41.550
comparisons were not significant. Direct PRMT5 target engagement was never established.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:51.050
COVID restrictions interrupted later protein-level follow-up. Our final report contained characterized imines, chemical observations,

00:02:51.050 --> 00:02:59.550
and unfinished biological questions. It did not contain the ring we had planned.
